{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1184 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "ea0b94eb1e689624b761399a2cb14999dbb9b38dc81374de3f5f8cb9484f9bab" :edb/db-before-t 1183 :edb/db-after-t 1184 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534496 50 #inst "2026-10-07T09:04:55.190Z" 13194139534496 true] [17592186105809 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291907 13194139534496 true] [17592186105809 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291913 13194139534496 true] [17592186105810 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291916 13194139534496 true] [17592186105810 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291925 13194139534496 true] [17592186105811 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291922 13194139534496 true] [17592186291907 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291908 13194139534496 true] [17592186291907 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291911 13194139534496 true] [17592186291907 1089 "q-302096" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291907 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534496 true] [17592186291907 1100 "Find the left-sided and the right-sided limits at $x=2$ for the function\n\n$$\ng(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-2 & \\text{ for }\\,x<2 \\\\ \\frac{3-\\sqrt{x+7}}{{x}^{2}-1} & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}g(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$ and $\\,$\n${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}g(x)=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291907 1113 #uuid "e6ea74d6-4e6e-569c-beb1-916ee0855aa7" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291907 1145 "Approaching from the left, we have $x<2,$ so we use the expression $g(x)={x}^{2}+x-2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}({x}^{2}+x-2) \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+2-2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApproaching from the right, we have $x\\ge 2,$ so we use the expression $g(x)=\\frac{3-\\sqrt{x+7}}{{x}^{2}-1}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}\\frac{3-\\sqrt{x+7}}{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{2+7}}{{2}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{9}}{4-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-3}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{3} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}g(x)=4,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}g(x)=0.\n$$" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291909 13194139534496 true] [17592186291908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291910 13194139534496 true] [17592186291908 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534496 true] [17592186291908 1041 "field-1" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291908 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291910 13194139534496 true] [17592186291908 1110 #uuid "891f76e1-63c8-5a59-825b-d32f074b5f11" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291909 1034 "3" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534496 true] [17592186291909 1111 #uuid "aea0dacb-d87b-5fd7-bc9c-a8eb5528949b" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291910 1034 "4" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534496 true] [17592186291910 1111 #uuid "71d04fdb-0d00-55ed-844a-a2c4185b844a" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291912 13194139534496 true] [17592186291911 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534496 true] [17592186291911 1041 "field-2" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291911 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291912 13194139534496 true] [17592186291911 1110 #uuid "e40b92ef-a03f-583b-8a51-53e5cb68f087" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291912 1034 "0" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534496 true] [17592186291912 1111 #uuid "c9cc27b4-bc6f-5cde-824b-08f458204387" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291913 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291914 13194139534496 true] [17592186291913 1089 "q-339885" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291913 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534496 true] [17592186291913 1100 "Find the left-sided limit at $x=\\pi $ for the function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+\\pi  & \\text{ for }\\,x<\\pi  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge \\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {\\pi }^{-}}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291913 1113 #uuid "56a3bc6b-7613-5691-931d-82b071475907" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291913 1145 "Approaching from the left, we have $x<\\pi ,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=x+\\pi .$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {\\pi }^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {\\pi }^{-}}(x+\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\pi +\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291915 13194139534496 true] [17592186291914 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534496 true] [17592186291914 1041 "field-1" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291914 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291915 13194139534496 true] [17592186291914 1110 #uuid "b9e1aeed-4d02-588e-a9ed-024eb0e5e3e8" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291915 1034 "2\\pi" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534496 true] [17592186291915 1111 #uuid "37007a92-d46b-5f53-9b1d-7f12e0198668" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291916 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291917 13194139534496 true] [17592186291916 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291920 13194139534496 true] [17592186291916 1089 "q-339938" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291916 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534496 true] [17592186291916 1100 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{3}+7 & \\text{ for }\\,x<-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{x-4}-1 & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$ and $\\,$\n${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}f(x)=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291916 1113 #uuid "e004bed6-6db1-5e30-858a-94d361c47d3f" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291916 1145 "Approaching $x=-2$ from the left, we have $x<-2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=(x+2)^{3}+7.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}[(x+2)^{3}+7] \\\\  & =(-2+2)^{3}+7 \\\\  & ={0}^{3}+7 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, approaching $x=4$ from the right, we have $x\\ge 4,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\sqrt{x-4}-1.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}(\\sqrt{x-4}-1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4-4}-1 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0}-1 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291917 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291918 13194139534496 true] [17592186291917 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291919 13194139534496 true] [17592186291917 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534496 true] [17592186291917 1041 "field-1" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291917 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291918 13194139534496 true] [17592186291917 1110 #uuid "d9f8e89e-ad7b-5ca0-b126-75ebd0893ac4" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291918 1034 "7" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291918 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534496 true] [17592186291918 1111 #uuid "0ac5718e-bc95-59a6-96e2-b0c9874e4a14" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291919 1034 "0" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291919 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534496 true] [17592186291919 1111 #uuid "c4755181-8e25-5da9-8c84-4cdf3a87d4f9" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291921 13194139534496 true] [17592186291920 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534496 true] [17592186291920 1041 "field-2" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291920 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291921 13194139534496 true] [17592186291920 1110 #uuid "389dab2b-0dcb-5527-baf5-9ee2f09551f1" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291921 1034 "-1" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534496 true] [17592186291921 1111 #uuid "66bedc67-9dc6-5efe-b558-de80d10ab6d7" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291922 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291923 13194139534496 true] [17592186291922 1089 "q-340291" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291922 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534496 true] [17592186291922 1100 "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}c\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x=2 \\\\ {x}^{3}-3\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ exists. What is the value of constant $c?$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291922 1113 #uuid "392b6b9a-c949-59f8-bea1-4e97e207c540" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291922 1145 "In order for ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ to exist, the left and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal.\n\n- Approaching from the left, we have $x<2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=c.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}c \\\\  & =c\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Approaching from the right, we have $x>2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)={x}^{3}-3.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}{x}^{3}-3 \\\\  & ={(2)}^{3}-3 \\\\  & =8-3 \\\\  & =5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the left and right-sided limits must be equal, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) \\\\ c & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291923 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291924 13194139534496 true] [17592186291923 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534496 true] [17592186291923 1041 "field-1" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291923 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291924 13194139534496 true] [17592186291923 1110 #uuid "aebce52a-a8f3-58e7-ae9d-066b29ee8bb0" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291924 1034 "5" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291924 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534496 true] [17592186291924 1111 #uuid "a199e1c1-57a6-56fe-935a-3200978e45cc" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291925 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291926 13194139534496 true] [17592186291925 1089 "q-67894" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291925 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534496 true] [17592186291925 1100 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{3}-2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le -1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,1\\le x\\le 10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291925 1113 #uuid "e54b505f-a312-5171-a5d1-68f09bb4fd20" 13194139534496 true] [17592186291925 1145 "To compute ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x),$ we must compute the left and right-sided limits separately.\n\nHowever, the left-si